<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import DealMenus from './lib/DealMenus.abide'
import dealMenus from './lib/DealMenus.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import NoteFormatting from './lib/NoteFormatting.abide'
import noteFormatting from './lib/NoteFormatting.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/menu', '/headless/toggle', '/headless/toggle-group']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealToolbar.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the toolbar is one tab stop, at its first item'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealToolbar.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the arrow keys move focus along the items, round the ends, past a disabled one'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealToolbar.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the item focused last is the one Tab comes back to'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealToolbar.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a field keeps its arrow keys, and a menu trigger its own'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealMenubar.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a menubar holds menu items opening menus, one of them a tab stop'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealMenubar.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('an open menu switches to the next on ArrowRight, and Escape returns to the bar'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Put a row of controls behind one tab stop">
        <p>Spread <code>toolbar</code> on the container and <code>item</code> on each control,
            beside any part of its own, such as a <code>toggle</code>'s button. Tab reaches the
            toolbar once, at the control focused last. The arrow keys move between the
            controls, passing over a disabled one. A field keeps its own arrow keys, and so does
            a control that handles them, such as a menu's button opening on ArrowDown.</p>
        <Example code={noteFormatting}><NoteFormatting /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Make a menubar of menus">
        <p>Given <code>role: 'menubar'</code>, each item is a menu item, so spread it on each
            menu's trigger, and hand every menu the bar's <code>id</code> as its
            <code>group</code>. The arrow keys walk the bar, ArrowDown opens a menu, and while one
            is open, ArrowLeft and ArrowRight switch to the menu beside it. Escape hands focus
            back to the bar.</p>
        <Example code={dealMenus}><DealMenus /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
